@* Shared presentational user-menu chrome — a native <details> dropdown, circuit-free (works on the
   static-SSR Identity pages AND interactive pages alike, no Blazor circuit). A "dumb" atom: the trigger
   icon and the menu items come in as @Trigger / @ChildContent, so it carries no auth knowledge and is
   shipped from the component module (NOT Auth) — reusable by any app, auth or not, the same way NavLinks
   shares the drawer's nav look. AppUserMenu (Auth) composes this with the account items + logout POST. *@

<details class="ux-user-menu">
    <summary class="ux-user-menu-trigger" title="@Title" aria-label="@Title">
        @Trigger
    </summary>
    <div class="ux-user-menu-panel" onclick="this.closest('details').removeAttribute('open')">
        @ChildContent
    </div>
</details>
